{"reference":"Nehemiah 9","book":"Nehemiah","chapter":9,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"What follows","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"The covenant announced at the close of this chapter is developed in the following material: leaders and people bind themselves to commitments concerning marriage, Sabbath commerce, temple tax, offerings, firstfruits, tithes, and support for God’s house. This places the long confession and historical prayer in a larger movement toward stated communal obligations.","verse_refs":["Nehemiah 10:1-39","Nehemiah 11:1-36","Nehemiah 12:1-26","Nehemiah 8:1-18"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_nehemiah_009_19601c3a319aef69b6584e22"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}